    "table csv": "Membrane,Gel composition,Si/Ge ratio in the gel,Support\nM1,0.195:19.5:1:438:50.6,100,Stainless steel\nM2,0.195:19.5:1:438:50.6,100,α-Al2O3\nM3,0.78:19.5:1:438:75,25,Stainless steel\nM4,0.78:19.5:1:438:75,25,Stainless steel\nM5,0.78:19.5:1:438:75,25,α-Al2O3\nM6,3.9:19.5:1:438:150,5,Stainless steel\nM7,3.9:19.5:1:438:150,5,Stainless steel\nM8,3.9:19.5:1:438:150,5,α-Al2O3",
    "extracted text": "From the experimental methods section:\n- Germanium-ZSM-5 membranes were prepared by in situ crystallization onto tubular porous supports (α-Al2O3 or Type 316 stainless steel)\n- The gel molar composition was Ge(C2H5O)4:SiO2:TPAOH:H2O:i-C3H7OH\n- Ludox AS 40 (silica sol) was used as the Si source\n- Tetra-propyl ammonium hydroxide (TPAOH) was used as the template\n- 2-propanol was added to the gel as a solvent\n- Zeolite synthesis was carried out at 458 K (185°C) for 24 h\n- A second layer was grown by the same procedure\n- After synthesis, the membranes were washed twice with distilled water, dried in a vacuum oven at 373 K, and then calcined in air at 753 K for 8 h with heating and cooling rates of 0.011 and 0.015 K/s, respectively",
    "property mapping": "- Gel composition (Molar ratio: Ge(C2H5O)4:SiO2:TPAOH:H2O:i-C3H7OH):\n  - Ge(C2H5O)4 → Ge\n  - SiO2 → Si\n  - TPAOH → OH and osda_names (tetra-propyl ammonium hydroxide)\n  - H2O → H2O\n  - i-C3H7OH → solvent (2-propanol)\n- Si/Ge ratio in the gel → ratio of Si to Ge\n- Support → substrate material\n- Temperature: 458 K → crystallization_temperature (185°C)\n- Time: 24 h → crystallization_time",
    "formula abbreviations": "- TPAOH: Tetra-propyl ammonium hydroxide, used as the structure directing agent (template)\n- i-C3H7OH: Isopropanol (2-propanol), used as a solvent\n- Ludox AS 40: Silica sol, used as the Si source\n- Ge(C2H5O)4: Germanium ethoxide, used as the Ge source\n- ZSM-5: Zeolite Socony Mobil-5, the product zeolite structure (MFI framework type)",
    "ratio calculations": "For each recipe, the gel composition is given in molar ratios as Ge(C2H5O)4:SiO2:TPAOH:H2O:i-C3H7OH. To normalize to Si = 1.0:\n\nM1, M2: 0.195:19.5:1:438:50.6\n- Si = 19.5 → normalized to 1.0\n- Ge = 0.195 → 0.195/19.5 = 0.01\n- TPAOH (osda) = 1 → 1/19.5 = 0.051\n- H2O = 438 → 438/19.5 = 22.462\n- i-C3H7OH = 50.6 → 50.6/19.5 = 2.595\n\nM3, M4, M5: 0.78:19.5:1:438:75\n- Si = 19.5 → normalized to 1.0\n- Ge = 0.78 → 0.78/19.5 = 0.04\n- TPAOH (osda) = 1 → 1/19.5 = 0.051\n- H2O = 438 → 438/19.5 = 22.462\n- i-C3H7OH = 75 → 75/19.5 = 3.846\n\nM6, M7, M8: 3.9:19.5:1:438:150\n- Si = 19.5 → normalized to 1.0\n- Ge = 3.9 → 3.9/19.5 = 0.2\n- TPAOH (osda) = 1 → 1/19.5 = 0.051\n- H2O = 438 → 438/19.5 = 22.462\n- i-C3H7OH = 150 → 150/19.5 = 7.692",
